# The release archive is what the DOI points at. It should contain what an
# Excel user actually needs -- the add-in, the module source, the licence, the
# changelog and the rendered manual -- and nothing that only matters to someone
# working inside the repository.
#
# EGAMMA.xlam is deliberately NOT export-ignored: it is the add-in the README
# tells people to install, so it must be present in the release archive and in
# the archival deposit made from it. docs/EGAMMA-VBA-manual.pdf is kept for the
# same reason. The Sphinx sources and build machinery that produce it are not,
# since nobody installing an Excel add-in is going to run sphinx-build.

docs/build     export-ignore
docs/source    export-ignore
docs/Makefile  export-ignore
docs/make.bat  export-ignore
.git*          export-ignore
